  "user": "Please look up transaction TX-0401 in my account records and verify its amount. Then explain which reason codes could apply; I have not yet told you what happened.",
  "answer": "**TX-0401 is confirmed at EUR 240.00.** Details from your account records:\n\n- **Date:** 2026-07-20\n- **Merchant:** TechMart Online\n- **Amount:** EUR 240.00 (outgoing card payment)\n- **Status:** Settled\n\nI also see a second payment to the same merchant, **TX-0402**, for EUR 240.00 on 2026-07-14, also settled. You may want to check whether that is related.\n\nThese are the dispute reason codes I can open, with what each covers:\n\n1. **duplicate_charge:** The same purchase was charged more than once. This could fit if TX-0401 and TX-0402 are two charges for one order.\n2. **fraud_card_not_present:** A card payment was made without your authorization and the card was not physically present (typical of online fraud).\n3. **unauthorized_debit:** A debit came out of your account that you did not authorize.\n4. **goods_not_received:** You paid for goods that were never delivered.\n5. **service_not_rendered:** You paid for a service that was never provided.\n\nWhich of these applies depends on what happened with this payment, which you haven't described yet. If you tell me, I'll check eligibility before anything is filed. No dispute has been opened.",
